meta {
  name: Update Interview Slot
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/interviews/slots/{{interviewSlotId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "venue": "Admin Block, Room 4"
  }
}

docs {
  Updates any subset of an interview slot's fields (mode, scheduled_date,
  start_time, end_time, duration_mins, campus_id, venue, interviewer_id,
  interviewer_email). No max_capacity — every slot is a fixed 1-on-1
  booking, not configurable.

  Changing interviewer_email only affects the Meet calendar event if it's
  updated before the event is first created (i.e. before any student has
  booked this slot) — see Create Interview Slot's docs for how/when that
  event actually gets created.

  interviewer_email is required whenever the slot's EFFECTIVE mode
  (this request's `mode` if provided, else the slot's existing mode) is
  "gmeet" — 400 ValidationError if it would end up empty, whether that's
  from explicitly clearing it or from switching `mode` to "gmeet" on a
  slot that never had one set.

  If scheduled_date or start_time is being changed, 400 ValidationError
  "Interview slots cannot be scheduled in the past" if the resulting
  scheduled_date + start_time combined is at or before the current time.

  409 ConflictError if changing `mode` to one that's currently disabled
  for this college — see Get Interview Settings / Update Interview
  Settings.

  404 "Campus not found" if `campus_id` is changed to one that doesn't
  belong to this college.
}
